# Files the static integration scan may not read for its marker vocabulary, because the
# vocabulary is the subject matter rather than a leftover. One glob per line.
#
# This list is for words that mean something real here and cannot be spelled another way.
# It is never the answer to a genuine TODO, stub or placeholder: those get implemented or
# deleted. Every entry names the term and why it has to stay.
#
# The cost is real and worth stating: an ignored file is skipped whole, so its silent
# failures and stray-file checks are skipped too. Keep this list short, and prefer renaming
# to listing whenever the word is ours to choose.

# This list itself, because naming the vocabulary is what every entry below is for and the
# scan would otherwise read its own reasons as findings.
.meow-verify-ignore

# "stub resolver" is RFC 1034's name for the resolver a client points at, and the timeouts,
# truncation rules and query flags in these files are written against its documented
# behaviour. Renaming it would leave the protocol reasoning describing something with no name.
internal/dnsfwd/dnsfwd.go
internal/dnsfwd/lookup.go
internal/dnsfwd/wire.go

# dnsmessage.RCodeNotImplemented is the standard library's constant for DNS RCODE 4, returned
# for a query class this resolver does not answer. The name is not ours to choose.
internal/dnsfwd/route.go

# http.StatusNotImplemented is the standard library's name for HTTP 501. It is given one
# name of ours here so the file that maps errors to statuses stays scanned.
internal/httpapi/status.go

# placeholder is the HTML attribute that renders the grey hint text inside an empty input.
# Every match in these files is that attribute on a real control.
ui/src/components/settings/controls.tsx
ui/src/components/access/RulesTable.tsx
ui/src/components/mode/RoutingCard.tsx
ui/src/components/DnsProfileDialog.tsx
ui/src/components/DnsBlockListDialog.tsx
ui/src/components/IpsFeedDialog.tsx
ui/src/pages/ActivityPage.tsx

# "fakenews" is StevenBlack's own name for one of the hosts files this catalog points at,
# and it is both the id in the settings and the path in the URL. Spelling it another way
# would name a list that does not exist.
internal/dnsblock/catalog.go

# The same names again, one file over: the ladder names Hagezi's fake-shop list by its id and
# says which rungs carry the fake-news category, so "fake" here is the subject rather than a
# leftover marker.
internal/dnsblock/presets.go

# "compress stub-v2" is openvpn's own spelling of the option that turns compression off, and
# this file reads openvpn configurations. The value is written by the servers whose files are
# pasted in, so it is not ours to spell another way.
internal/config/ovpnfile.go

# A lockfile nobody writes by hand: the marker turns up inside npm's base64 integrity
# hashes. The scan excludes a lockfile at the repo root and this one is a directory down.
*/package-lock.json

# placeholder is a field of GitHub's issue-form schema, which renders the grey hint text
# inside an empty input. The word is the schema's, not ours.
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature_request.yml
